# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} Someone or something that tends to inspire [[mobs]]; something [[controversial]] or [[provocative]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1917|title={{w|A Book of Prefaces}}|author=H. L. Mencken|authorlink=H. L. Mencken|chapter=Joseph Conrad|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/19355/pg19355-images.html|passage=They proceed steadily from studies of human character and destiny, the proper business of the novelist, to mere outpourings of social and economic panaceas, the proper business of leader writers, chautauquas '''rabble-rousers''' and hedge politicians.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Motoko Rich|title=A Yale Professor Suggested Mass Suicide for Old People in Japan. What Did He Mean?|work=The New York Times|date=2023-02-12|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/02/12/world/asia/japan-elderly-mass-suicide.html|issn=0362-4331|author2=Hikari Hida|passage=He often appears with Gen X '''rabble-rousers''' like Hiroyuki Nishimura, a celebrity entrepreneur and owner of 4chan, the online message board where some of the internet’s most toxic ideas bloom, and Takafumi Horie, a trash-talking entrepreneur who once went to prison for securities fraud.}}

